A||||6||JetroGT||People who claim they owned a Fiero.||||13||
Z||000000||JetroGT||02-10-2000||05:01 AM||||<BR>Once in a while I'll wear one of my Dells run shirts or a N.I.F.E. shirt to work and usually no one really says anything. Then a couple days ago one of the new guys in the department was saying that he used to own one, "A 88 GT Notch Back.". So I brought my Fiero photo album to work the next day. Started off with the different hood decales that people had done along with some air brush pictures. Then I was showing him some pictures of the front compartment. He says, " I rember all of thoughs wires, all around the engine compartment". <BR>And this other guy was blaiming the Fiero for cutting open his leg. He said that when driving his car up on some metal ramps one of the ramps poped up and sliced his leg open. He also went on to say that he kept hitting things with his car in the snow, and that his alingment was all messed up. Then he said that every time that he came to a stop light it would die on him. He said that it was an automatic. Then went on to say that he solved that by unplugging some sensor on the transmission, probably the TCC. <BR>Thoughs poor poor Fieros. Isn't their a law about the mistreatment of fieros?||||reg||13
Z||000002||Scott2M4||02-10-2000||08:56 AM||||Monkey - you were in a bar the other day and you didn't call me!?  I'm hurt!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||02-10-2000||09:15 AM||||My brother was up at the post office the other day and a dude told him "Nice ride, I have an '88 Formula now, but I had one when the first came out <I>back in '73</I>."<P>Maybe he thought it was a Firebird, although I believe Firebird first appeared in '69.<P>||||reg||1
